    {
     "_comment": "Gate B: honor off-store ExtensionSettings/ExtensionInstallForcelist on UNMANAGED Chrome. PolicyLoaderWin::LoadChromePolicy guards its FilterSensitivePolicies(&policy) call with ShouldFilterSensitivePolicies() (inlined to `cmp dword[rsi+0x18],1 ; jg skip`). FilterSensitivePolicies [BLOCKED]-prefixes force-install entries whose update_url != the Chrome Web Store, so on an unmanaged browser a self-hosted extension is dropped (chrome://policy: 'ignored - not from a trusted source'). Flipping the jg to jmp always skips the filter, so platform-source ExtensionSettings is honored. Direction-only flip (same target, no call removed). Blast radius: all sensitive platform policies are honored on unmanaged Chrome (setting those registry keys already requires admin). required: this gate is enforced, so a build where it does not match reports partial rather than enabling MV2 without ExtensionSettings. The other FilterSensitivePolicies caller is the chrome://policy/test local-test loader (not this platform path).",
     "name": "LoadChromePolicy: skip FilterSensitivePolicies (honor off-store ExtensionSettings on unmanaged Chrome)",
     "kind": "short",
     "jgRVA": "0x0205653F",
     "jgOff": 12,
     "expectedMatches": 1,
     "sig": "488BBC2420010000837E18017F0A488D4C2448"
    }
   ]
  },
