   "_comment": "macOS Apple Silicon, 153.0.8010.36+ (current stable). Chrome 153 keeps the 152 (un-shifted) Extension field layout, so the four bcond gates are byte-identical to 152-macos-arm64. The FilterSensitivePolicies cbz sig is intentionally trimmed to end at `mov x20,x0`, dropping the trailing `ldrsb w8,[sp,#N]` frame slot: that spill offset is the ONLY unmasked build-variant field (BL/CBZ/B displacements are already masked by the matcher), and it drifts on point-release codegen (moved #0x6f->#0x8f 152->153, and shifted again .36->.37, which stranded the old 24-byte sig on a partial 152 match that missed this off-store gate). The trimmed 20-byte sig is verified UNIQUE in .text on CfT 153.0.8010.36 (mov x0,x20 / bl / cbz w0 / b / mov x20,x0). Derived from CfT (unbranded) -- re-verify against a real Chrome.app.",
